10. Philosophical Position

The framework adopts neither the assumption that scientific theories must always be mutually consistent nor the assumption that every contradiction indicates a new discovery.

\boxed{\text{Scientific tension is information about model adequacy}}

A tension may dissolve because context was incomplete, measurements were incompatible, claims concerned different regimes, one study was erroneous, or evidence was insufficient. It may also survive these checks. A persistent, well-supported tension is then a candidate frontier of scientific ignorance.

The Architecture of Ignorance asks:

\text{What is missing?}

The Tension Engine asks:

\text{What does not fit?}

Together:

\boxed{\text{Scientific Ignorance} \;=\; \text{Missing Knowledge} \;+\; \text{Unresolved Tension}}

producing two complementary memories

M_G = \text{Gap Memory}, \qquad M_T = \text{Tension Memory},

with combined discovery controller

\mathcal{C} = f(M_G, M_T, \mathcal{K}).

